54-23787-01 is the ALphastation 250 system board.

Maximum memory: 192 MB (384 MB when 64-MB SIMMs are available) 
Upgrade options: 16-MB, 32-MB, 64-MB, or 128-MB 
Memory options are pairs of SIMMs: 
16-MB option consisting of two 8-MB SIMMs 
32-MB option consisting of two 16-MB SIMMs 
64-MB option consisting of two 32-MB SIMMs 
128-MB option consisting of two 64-MB SIMMs 
Always add SIMMs in sets of 4,  into one of two available memory banks

The system requires 72-pin parity SIMMs that have an access time of 70
ns 

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

NOTE:
If you are adding memory and adding a drive to the upper bay of the
inner storage area at the same time, add the memory SIMMs while the
drive bracket is removed for easier installation. If you are adding
memory and adding a drive to the lower bay of the inner storage area
at the same time, however, remove the SIMMs. Then you can add the
lower-bay drive, followed by the SIMMs.  

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 


