Check your hardware first.

The NCR chipset on the Alphaserver 2100 is used for the internal fast
SCSI bus that includes he internal CDROM and internal Dat tape . It
can  be and usually is , routed to the Internal Storageworks disks .
You should be able to see all the devices on the bus at the SRM
console. 
At the >>> prompt type     SHOW DEVICE 
Make sure there are no SCSI ID conflicts between the storaworks disks
and cdrom and tape. Also this internal scsi bus uses 2.8meters of
cable when attached to the internal Storageworks shelf. You will need
to termiante the SCSI bus at the  50 pin hi density connector on the
rear of the system.
 DO not add any external devices if you are using the internal shelf
on this bus, as it will exceed the 3m lenth restriction on fast scsi.


Brian C

