Perhaps that was a difficult way to phrase it.  Tru64 will *only* run on 
Alpha machines, but it won't run on *every* alpha machine.  Supposedly.  
IMHO, if you want to run it, you can.

>> And is it true that you can only boot it from SCSI disks?
>
>Don't know. Would be no problem for us since we have only SCSI.

The SRM only supports boot from scsi disks, however, in *some* systems, if 
you set os_type to vms, it enables an ide-scsi emulation driver which in 
practice lets you boot from ide devices.  
If you want to do that, ask if your specific machine will support that, and 
don't only ask here.  Also ask in the tru64 group.  They know a lot there, 
too.


