Zerodiv102 wrote:
> 
> I am trying to install RH7 on a PWS433a. Ive read that SRM was the easiest way
> to do so so I switched the console to Digital-Unix SRM and now when my computer
> boots it goes to a blue screen and only shows"ea.e9.e8.e7.e6". Any ideas what
> wrong or how to switch back to alphaBIOS?

Nothing is really wrong. The "ea.e9.e8.e7.e6" etc showing up on your
screen is normal SRM self test. When the SRM console ">>>" appears
(after the completed self test) you need to set the console variable
os_type to NT and do a hard reset. Then you'll get AlphaBIOS back and
you can continue installing Linux.

In SRM console you can always get some help with just typing "help" at
the >>> prompt.

Regards,

Kari


