I noticed others have struggled with this problem too, but I haven't seen
the solution in this forum (but I was able to deduct a solution from the
redhat mailing list archive). Perhaps it will be of assistance to others.

Alpha XL 266 with ARC console, SCSI disk & CD-rom. Due to the arc console it
won't boot from CD.

Option one is to create a milo boot disk, a generic boot disk and a ramdisk
boot disk. Getting milo up and running was a breeze, but I could not boot
the generic image because milo could not handle the filesystem (fat v12).
Didn't find a solution for this.

Option two is to use the same milo boot disk and usemilo to load a boot
image from the cdrom. Using the command line given in the help file resulted
in the following error message: 'Kernel Panic: No init found.  Try passing
init= option to kernel'. It took me quite some time to find the solution and
I had to piece together contributions from multiple authors, but this line
worked for me:

boot scd0:/kernels/vmlinux.gz root=/dev/scd0 initrd=/images/ramdisk.img text

Please notice the text bit, because otherwise my system kept rebooting as
soon as it tried to switch to graphical mode.

Regards,

Andries






