You probably have an Alphastation 250 or 255 , These use 2 banks of 4
simms each ( total of 8 simm slots) The AS250 has the top 3 simm slots
slightly offset to the rest. The AS255 has all simms in a straight
row.

Found this info on led codes.
xxxx xxxx  all on
 F       F


Alphastation 250    
>     LED Code      Meaning                                                   
|>                                                                             
|>        FA         memory test 1 failed                                      
|>        F9         memory test 2 failed                                      
|>        F8         memory test 3 failed                                      
|>        F7         memory test 4 failed                                      
|>        F2         DROM and flashROM corrupted                               
|>        DE         memory test failed                                        
|>        DD         flashROM ID test failed                                   
|>        DC         NVRAM test failed                                         
|>        DB         SCSI test failed                                          
|>        DA         PCI/ISA bridge test failed                                
|>        D9         TOY test failed                                           
|>        D8         keyboard controller test failed                           
|>        D7         Super I/O chip test failed                                
|>                   (floppy, parallel port, COM ports)                        
|>        D6         interrupt test failed       
|>        D0         power-on selftest passed, DROM console running            
|>        E2         floppy load failed                                        
|>        E1         flashROM load failed                                      
|>        20         machine check occurred                                    
|>        E5         All OK      



ALphastation 255 codes


Console starting (FF). 
Initialize idle PCB (FE). 

Initialize semaphores (FD). 

Initialize heap (dynamic memory) (FC, FB, and FA). 

Initialize driver structures (F9). 

Initialize idle process PID (F8). 

Initialize file system (F7). 

Initialize timer data structures (F6). 

Lower the IPL (F5). 

Enter the idle loop (F4). 

Memory configuration (EF). 

Initialize IRQ vector table and configure PCI bus (DF). 

DDB startup parts 1, 2, and 3, and locate HWRPB (EE, ED, and EC) 

Test memory greater then 8 MB (EB). 

DDB startup part 4 (EA). 

Set keyboard type according to language variable (E9). 

Initialize environment variables (E8). 

Initialize SCSI (E7). 

DDB startup part 5 (E6). 

Show version and console idle (normal final state) (E5). 



               

