To boot the CD,

boot dka4 -fl 0

However, a 500a can have hardware not supported by SRM or X, most common is
the Adaptec SCSI Controller
and a TGA video(X), both of which were supported by NT, the video may work
till the installer starts, then hang, if this happens  instead of -fl 0
enter -fl "initrd=images/ramdisk.img expert text"  (with the quotes)

If you burned the CD, make sure you did not use RW media but CD-R media,
some old reader do not like the CD-RW media, i have a few PWS's like that.

JJ

