Hello,

I just threw together a page at

http://www.sunperf.com/SRM-Alpha-Linux-Install.html

also at

http://www.shana-sewing.com/norm/as200/as200.html

is an older page but should give some good info on dual booting
with NT. If you want to get rid of NT use the first. I recommend
trashing NT on Alpha. It is not supported anymore and it is hard to
get any applications to work, even with FX32!.

You will have to get rid of the DOS partition label so that SRM can
boot. It needs a BSD Label. You will loose all data, so back it up.

Compaq's guide said to scrub the partition table by doing the
following at the SRM prompt.

>>>chmod +w dka*
>>>exer -a w dka0 &
>>>show_status

and watch until Bytes Written is 8MB (one cylinder).
This did not work on my box so I did the dd command
on my page.

Hope it helps.

Norm.


