I recently upgraded RH6.2 to RH7.0, here's what I did:

a.     Copy the vmlinux.gz onto a floppy (it will fit just about right)

b.     Copy the kernels/ramdisk.img onto a floppy using rawrite
        c:\rawrite.exe -f ramdisk.img -d a: -n (i.e. I assume you have
access to both rawrite and kernels/ramdisk.img from your RH7.0 cd rom)

c.     Insert the vmlinux.gz into the floppy drive after booting MILO or
whatever till you get to the prompt.

d.     Issue the following command:

        boot fd0:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1

e.     The system will prompt you to insert the boot floppy, where in you
insert the floppy containg the ramdisk.img and press enter.

f.     The system will go through the installation process (i.e.
upgrade/fresh install, where in you can specify where the distribution set
is)

g.     Once the installation is complete, you can set the OS partition to
boot from the new kernel - which is

        vmlinux-2.2.17-4 (I believe).

h.     Also, make sure you install the security patches to RH7.0.

Mohan








