So do you install the ramdisk floppy?

The ramdisk image is a gz'd root file system for the install, it loads into
memory, So you have a mini linux fs running out of memory. After it thinks
its loaded, or times out, it tries to open a console (/dev/console) but if
the ramdisk was not loaded, it does not exist, giving you the error  "Cannot
open initial console"

in 7.0 the ramdisk is loaded  via the "initrd" command

Try rawriting the ramdisk.img to a floppy and try the following command

>>>boot fd0 -fi vmlinux.gz  -fl "initrd=/dev/fd0"

JJ
